flowchart TB
    accTitle: Reset current credentials with the Recovery Key
    accDescr: The reset wizard validates the current Recovery Key against config v4 and authenticates the vault before collecting replacements. The new Master Password, newly saved Recovery Key and newly verified Authenticator must differ from the previous credentials. Core preserves the existing DEK and vault ciphertext, commits verified new config wrappers, increments credential revision, and returns to sign-in without workspace authority.
    forgot["Sign-in screen:\nForgot Master Password"] --> key["SECRET: current Recovery Key"]:::secret
    key --> verify{"Unwrap DEK and\nauthenticate current vault?"}
    verify -->|Invalid / unsupported config| reject["Stop; keep current credentials"]:::danger
    verify -->|Valid| password["Choose and confirm\na new Master Password"]
    password --> replacement["Generate a fresh Recovery Key\nConfirm it is saved outside this device"]
    replacement --> auth["Set up replacement Authenticator\nVerify its current six-digit code"]
    auth --> checks{"All replacements valid\nand different from previous credentials?"}
    checks -->|No / cancel| reject
    checks -->|Yes| rewrap["Keep same DEK and .storage ciphertext\nCreate new Master and Recovery wrappers"]
    rewrap --> config["Encrypt new sign-in Authenticator\nIncrement credential revision"]
    config --> commit[["Cryptographically verify staged state\nCommit config with unchanged storage"]]
    commit -->|Failure| rollback["Report failure\nAttempt pair rollback"]:::danger
    commit -->|Success| login["Clear session and compatibility token\nReturn to sign-in with new credentials"]:::good
    classDef secret fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#0f172a
    classDef danger fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#991b1b
    classDef good fill:#f0fdf4,stroke:#16a34a,color:#14532d
